<title>GERMANY: Depfa 96 oper profit after provs up 45 pct.</title>
<headline>Depfa 96 oper profit after provs up 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    467    vs 321</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    186    vs 141</p>
<p>    Dividend					1.40   up 0.20 marks</p>
<p>    Earnings per share			  5.12   vs 4.59 marks</p>
<p>    Return on Equity			    7.3    vs 6.4 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Deutsche Pfandbrief-und Hypothekenbank AG. The return on equity figure given is an after-tax figure. The EPS figure given is calculated using the DVFA method.</p>
<p>DePfa said that its 1997 EPS, using the DVFA method, would not be less than six marks.</p>
</text>
